{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.729729Z","id":"afa8b528e7374450a20a041d28d29d75deae1d2b3e7525ce1dcdbfe7fecc4df4","body":{"detail":"Seen in Linux perf runs: a single commit held up by the disk. The writer runs WAL with SQLite's default synchronous=FULL, so every commit syncs the WAL, and the background PASSIVE checkpoint runs every CHECKPOINT_INTERVAL (2 s). Every delivery of a write waits on its commit, so one slow commit moves a whole cluster of deliveries (scripts/perf-clients.py:23-29 explains how the realtime gate copes).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":83},"content_hash":"19a1b1cc49fe118705a9d82f6b9227495d66a06ae11378ed14f24dfb809e7ed5"},"suggested_fix":"Measure commit times on Linux with synchronous=NORMAL (durable across a crash of the process, not of the machine, in WAL mode) and with a different checkpoint cadence before choosing.","summary":"On Linux, store commits occasionally take 25 to 120 ms","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970746Z","id":"e186fa5eb94b4d4745bc582f181edaca45f47ef4742794b12e457f31b20db499","body":{"detail":"check_person_name compares the token form only with the owner, connected unrevoked persons and live agents. Extending it to every viewer row breaks two behaviours the store tests pin: a revoked person's name is free again (people.rs revoking_a_grant_ends_its_sessions_and_revoking_a_person_keeps_history) and an unredeemed invite frees the name (an_unredeemed_invites_person_goes_back_to_a_viewer). With the rule unenforced, the old cookie of a revoked 'Mia', or a LAN viewer who named themselves 'Jun' before Jun was invited, comments under the same name as the connected person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":350},"end":{"line":375},"content_hash":"a1f8247d6233f381c1f7bd1582a76e16b34dc4494d83697c90b2ce355cfddd91"},"suggested_fix":"Decide whether revoked and lapsed persons' rows count as existing viewers for §9.6; then either check all viewer rows (and rename or mark the older one) or amend §9.6.","summary":"A new person may take the name of an existing plain LAN viewer, a revoked person or an unredeemed invite's person, though spec §9.6 says a new person cannot be named after an existing viewer's name","tags":["status:needs-decision","spec:9.6","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970963Z","id":"ebd868e7580dc68c488bfac1f17d29a446dfa3a85b3d30f8cb5b27099ac4a203","body":{"detail":"Spec §11 refuses naming a person to a live agent's name (409 name_taken), and §9.6 refuses viewers the owner's or a person's name, but set_owner_name only checks the name's form. Checking it would change single-owner behaviour that §19 does not list, so it is left as it was.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":389},"end":{"line":392},"content_hash":"6c717bdc42d7c2983ff9d8169636be81e1725987de1a1689ff487a84a0324a3c"},"summary":"The owner can rename themselves to a live agent's name or a connected person's name; nothing refuses it","tags":["status:needs-decision","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.971168Z","id":"a7e7b5c6856d3630e36f7641bb0f0bfc14b51dd7d43458726e7c0de07f385cc7","body":{"detail":"send_in skips every viewer comment that has a feedback row for any target, so POST …/threads/<tid>/send {to} after the thread went to another agent inserts no rows for the new one, though it becomes the thread's target. Store::send_to_named (used for @name) instead checks rows per target, so the two ways of sending to one agent differ.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":190},"content_hash":"fa071b0439a92e52e404930d6c2d65a5073dd91f44b9ab2dd0c480371df7f5f9"},"suggested_fix":"Decide whether a send with to should, like @name, give the named agent every comment it has no row for (spec §12 makes it the thread's owner).","summary":"A send with to on a thread whose comments already have rows gives the named agent nothing","tags":["spec:12","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:09.122041Z","id":"6d73133464fbe924b4046f650e56047664681d4dbffa53ff8c285b63a56fcf62","body":{"detail":"Checking only viewers with no invites row (NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM invites WHERE viewer_id = v.id)) and not revoked keeps the two pinned behaviours (revoking_a_grant_ends_its_sessions_and_revoking_a_person_keeps_history, an_unredeemed_invites_person_goes_back_to_a_viewer), and stops a LAN viewer who named themselves 'Jun' first from sharing the name with the person Jun. The 409 should point the owner at inviting that viewer ({viewer}, spec section 6.2) instead. A lapsed {viewer} invitee's name also stays free under this rule.","kind":"comment","references":"e186fa5eb94b4d4745bc582f181edaca45f47ef4742794b12e457f31b20db499","summary":"Reviewer's recommendation: enforce section 9.6 against viewer rows no invite made, and keep revoked and lapsed invitees' names free","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:09.122080Z","id":"131f80f14301f0003a7c26ea2e76e3131a90b4d7d2b22f683e60b45815838a96","body":{"detail":"Section 11 reserves the owner's display name from agents and refuses a person a live agent's name; the reverse for the owner is the same rule. Without it the owner named 'web' makes '@web' both a mention of the owner and a send to the agent web, and an owner named 'Sam' shares a name with the person Sam in agents' author lines. In a single-owner install it refuses only a live agent's exact name, so the section 19 change is one line.","kind":"comment","references":"ebd868e7580dc68c488bfac1f17d29a446dfa3a85b3d30f8cb5b27099ac4a203","summary":"Reviewer's recommendation: refuse the owner a live agent's name or a connected person's token form (409 name_taken), and add it to spec section 19 item 8","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:50.467898Z","id":"3992d3af163cdf12b5036616ab013f2867e663176be2e2f1dfbddc42d9f02f6e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dbf0fe7","summary":"The owner decided: \"refuse a new person's name only when it is held by a viewer who was never invited and isn't revoked (NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM invites WHERE viewer_id = v.id)). Revoked and lapsed names stay free. The 409 says to invite that viewer instead.\" Implemented in dbf0fe7 (check_person_name; spec §9.6 amended); store test sessions::tests::names::a_new_person_cannot_take_an_uninvited_viewers_name covers the refusal, its message, inviting that viewer, a revoked person's name and a lapsed invite's name.","supersedes":"e186fa5eb94b4d4745bc582f181edaca45f47ef4742794b12e457f31b20db499","tags":["reason:fixed","status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:50.467966Z","id":"78611b98322ef9217c8171c9efffe8826e8786e14a7bf100aa6e62124a5499f5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dbf0fe7","summary":"The owner decided: \"refuse the owner a live agent's name or a connected person's name with 409 name_taken. Add the line to §19's list of single-owner changes.\" Implemented in dbf0fe7 (set_owner_name runs check_viewer_name; §19 item 8 amended); tests sessions::tests::names::the_owner_cannot_take_a_live_agents_or_a_persons_name and api_viewers::the_owner_cannot_take_a_live_agents_name. The single-owner golden regenerated byte-identical.","supersedes":"ebd868e7580dc68c488bfac1f17d29a446dfa3a85b3d30f8cb5b27099ac4a203","tags":["reason:fixed","status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:37:09.171936Z","id":"bfcb3e120098d9fd1e28f5397a8d93dfe8dffabdd9c3631d04e1c7339e8c6509","body":{"detail":"checked_name serves every display name: LAN viewers', the owner's (set_owner_name) and people's. At ca9c8bc upsert_viewer refuses 'Dmitri Дмитрий', 'Ivan (Иван)', 'Αλέξης Smith' and 'محمد Ali' as mixed script, and 'שרה\\u{200F}' (a right-to-left mark) as a control character, with no person connected. Spec section 19 item 8 lists only the reserved-name refusals. Stored names are untouched; only setting one is refused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":37},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"b9e698544a416a42d027587d14fd5414197b30ab38a560bae92e1d6ba878c09c"},"suggested_fix":"Either add an item to section 19 (display names with a bidirectional control or mixing scripts are 400 invalid_name), or narrow the refusal to names whose confusable skeleton (UTS #39) equals the owner's or a connected person's token form, which leaves bilingual names alone.","summary":"The mixed-script and bidi-control refusals change single-owner installs beyond spec section 19's list: bilingual names and RTL names with a mark are now 400","tags":["review","spec:19","spec:9.6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:37:22.293907Z","id":"0da5f34770c3d2f0de3a44ce580682294f03c9d516c3bf17d33b632ff06993f1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:10b9ae1","summary":"Fixed in 10b9ae1 under the coordinator's revised ruling (not an owner decision): display names may use any script or mix of scripts; checked_name refuses only bidirectional embedding, override and isolate controls (U+202A-U+202E, U+2066-U+2069), with its own message; LRM, RLM and ALM are allowed and dropped when comparing; protection is by collision: names::CollisionKeys (UTS #39 skeletons from unicode-security) makes a name name_taken when it looks like the owner's, a connected person's or a live agent's. Tests: crates/clax-server/tests/api_viewers.rs names_that_render_as_a_persons_or_the_owners_are_refused accepts 'Dmitri Дмитрий', 'Ivan (Иван)', 'محمد Ali' and a Hebrew name with RLM and refuses or collides on every earlier probe; names::tests::look_alike_names_meet. Spec §9.6 and §19 item 8 describe the rule; names valid before stay valid apart from collisions with a protected name and the bidi controls, which item 8 lists.","supersedes":"bfcb3e120098d9fd1e28f5397a8d93dfe8dffabdd9c3631d04e1c7339e8c6509","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:37:22.293980Z","id":"f269d31494b5970a9be7d87dff570af165d0dae39bbee96f96c4012bf3361e56","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3992d3af163cdf12b5036616ab013f2867e663176be2e2f1dfbddc42d9f02f6e","summary":"This resolve records the owner's decision, which the owner gave in the coordinating session on 2026-10-10; the owner did not write the record, an agent did.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:37:22.294001Z","id":"510184bf723b4b40d848a9ed9c94034b16a1cea4f168da2a7a5deff0f2afcc38","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"78611b98322ef9217c8171c9efffe8826e8786e14a7bf100aa6e62124a5499f5","summary":"This resolve records the owner's decision, which the owner gave in the coordinating session on 2026-10-10; the owner did not write the record, an agent did.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:45:31.444744Z","id":"ec6c19a00b08c581fd9d385af0290dda58e639840a7f9fac67be3bc5dcf7bea8","body":{"detail":"At 8446429: upsert_viewer(lan, 'Аlex') with no owner name succeeds; set_owner_name('Alex') then succeeds too, and both names stand. An agent registering from repository web is named 'web' beside a LAN viewer 'wеb'. New people are covered (check_person_name refuses a look-alike held by an uninvited viewer). The owner usually names themselves late, on a first comment, so pre-squatting is the likely order.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":83},"content_hash":"3326bd9d00ba88c8520dc5a9e6fb72f49445c3a5ea484cda21e23304bd36a6e4"},"suggested_fix":"Mark it where names are shown: an unconnected viewer whose name looks like a protected name is flagged in the shell and in agent author lines (with spec section 9.6's '(not connected)', Task 17), rather than refusing the owner their own name.","summary":"The look-alike check runs only when the later name is set: a LAN viewer who took 'Аlex' before the owner named themselves 'Alex', or 'wеb' before an agent web went live, keeps it","tags":["review","spec:9.6","revisit:task-17","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:45:31.444837Z","id":"0a1233c8ae3203f3c8825c45e7c5ed9d19b5ea5ebfe6c5236e0a841e5ed83ddc","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"78611b98322ef9217c8171c9efffe8826e8786e14a7bf100aa6e62124a5499f5","summary":"Closed by an agent on the owner's decision, recorded 2026-10-10.","supersedes":"510184bf723b4b40d848a9ed9c94034b16a1cea4f168da2a7a5deff0f2afcc38","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:45:31.444917Z","id":"be58e9c19d3f54c389bce12f6fbe51da9e4ab3e986fb2627f45a26bb2d0f6b52","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3992d3af163cdf12b5036616ab013f2867e663176be2e2f1dfbddc42d9f02f6e","summary":"Closed by an agent on the owner's decision, recorded 2026-10-10.","supersedes":"f269d31494b5970a9be7d87dff570af165d0dae39bbee96f96c4012bf3361e56","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.618828Z","id":"92e4398f5b69223950271250988c91747dfa19ede18d380b3589510945ab8e70","body":{"detail":"send_in skips every viewer comment that has a feedback row for any target, so POST …/threads/<tid>/send {to} after the thread went to another agent inserts no rows for the new one, though it becomes the thread's target. Store::send_to_named (used for @name) instead checks rows per target, so the two ways of sending to one agent differ.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":190},"content_hash":"4d26296fbd266f8c3776482cc19d813aa85b511f7becea3cb9a44c98292d4c92"},"suggested_fix":"Decide whether a send with to should, like @name, give the named agent every comment it has no row for (spec §12 makes it the thread's owner).","summary":"A send with to on a thread whose comments already have rows gives the named agent nothing","supersedes":"a7e7b5c6856d3630e36f7641bb0f0bfc14b51dd7d43458726e7c0de07f385cc7","tags":["spec:12","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.618964Z","id":"2c3182731c84d005ef66708718194afec212d5003d1576e31cd87e7a6c985bcd","body":{"detail":"At 8446429: upsert_viewer(lan, 'Аlex') with no owner name succeeds; set_owner_name('Alex') then succeeds too, and both names stand. An agent registering from repository web is named 'web' beside a LAN viewer 'wеb'. New people are covered (check_person_name refuses a look-alike held by an uninvited viewer). The owner usually names themselves late, on a first comment, so pre-squatting is the likely order.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":83},"content_hash":"d5b22f70e442ee22c3d2c8cecd9fb469a2ebea4e76d3e6523fb7899692b93d12"},"suggested_fix":"Mark it where names are shown: an unconnected viewer whose name looks like a protected name is flagged in the shell and in agent author lines (with spec section 9.6's '(not connected)', Task 17), rather than refusing the owner their own name.","summary":"The look-alike check runs only when the later name is set: a LAN viewer who took 'Аlex' before the owner named themselves 'Alex', or 'wеb' before an agent web went live, keeps it","supersedes":"ec6c19a00b08c581fd9d385af0290dda58e639840a7f9fac67be3bc5dcf7bea8","tags":["review","spec:9.6","revisit:task-17","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.258890Z","id":"5819144b476b3e759440c7c18ed72d8ca312b9bc46c9f3248a53d12ed46cf472","body":{"detail":"record_tool_call selects audit_events by call_id alone. Since ea4daf0 a grant's x-clax-call counts, so a call_id sent by an agent of another machine joins an owner agent's tool.call (its produced list and the artifact the call belongs to) if the IDs collide. Call IDs are agent-minted ULIDs, so a collision needs a guessed or leaked ID; the risk is low, but the call index now spans credentials.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":437},"end":{"line":444},"content_hash":"fe045ef41d3509d21b9747bf185f6947ff224dd134b75f9b68571e5644ef801e"},"suggested_fix":"Filter produced by the reporting session (session_id = the report's session; NULL session and the same actor for the sessionless /api/tool-calls).","summary":"tool.call's produced list joins every event with the call_id, whoever recorded it","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.259041Z","id":"92eb68c6c559ff8100c7ff88faf9a9b9716b133ad410c3d630689dcff97d5883","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1959},"end":{"line":1970},"content_hash":"abcc7e8301e6907a066149ce4e4072d50030d68fe3a10a12f5af4a65b3c499db"},"suggested_fix":"Record invite.revoke (by expiry, actor system:expiry) for each invite the sweep finds lapsed, and person.rights {person, rights: null} for each row release_unconnected changes; add both to section 6.13.","summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.259151Z","id":"bb251370ba0151754f40547c74592b97d41884be98064bcc45c5d984fdb22c1b","body":{"detail":"For flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1066},"end":{"line":1080},"content_hash":"a055d17fb6d13921d9565129c8f0b702f534ab8d657151596b97465c24004831"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T14:21:06.259249Z","id":"a40cabad94e6b3b1c0cf1c0ff82e5a41cc4de0f9bc78a6e7cf891fcbaed965e9","body":{"detail":"Registration derives a name from the repository and branch (spec section 11) without an event; session.start's body is harness, harness_session_id, cwd, transcript_path and pid. The first agent.name then reports previous: <derived name> with no earlier event naming it, and an @name in a comment cannot be tied to its session from the journal alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":154},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"2531645c1bbef5581474f3318cd70a2a599ab739af3be8223fbe8da994159a5b"},"suggested_fix":"Add name (classed as a name for redaction) to session.start and session.join bodies, and say so in audit spec section 6.8.","summary":"A session's derived name is never recorded, so agent.name's previous names a value the journal never held","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T15:49:07.081042Z","id":"69843dde6d973a5720977e84521e222f75d87c2089e76fd10557ee755d4712db","body":{"detail":"M17 lists rights, narrowing and elevation changes among the bump sources. Every source with a store write today calls Store::visibility_changed and is pinned by store::approvals::tests::every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once. The per-agent narrow and elevate routes arrive later; each, and any new write that sets viewers.person or person_revoked_at, must mark the change too, or the owner's fast path (Store::owner_sees_all, cached per generation) and rights caches go stale.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":194},"end":{"line":202},"content_hash":"c28dd7bfcd2dbdb2d9681cc69bc620ba9b5058d3016a9616178a80c1c35b54a2"},"suggested_fix":"Call self.visibility_changed() in the store methods that write sessions.narrow_json and elevate_json, and add them to every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once.","summary":"Agent narrowing and elevation do not bump the visibility generation yet: no write of sessions.narrow_json or elevate_json exists","tags":["visibility","revisit:when agent narrowing and elevation are stored","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T15:50:05.978925Z","id":"79623e38cfcc9cd895a38f0b5b0f4429c5d515932313f4f5f1e18ccc4002694b","body":{"detail":"For flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1076},"end":{"line":1090},"content_hash":"a055d17fb6d13921d9565129c8f0b702f534ab8d657151596b97465c24004831"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","supersedes":"bb251370ba0151754f40547c74592b97d41884be98064bcc45c5d984fdb22c1b","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T15:50:05.979251Z","id":"8e23afd215d98a3120cf8544db13284d7cde1b79ca73fc49e8c1c9d01a17fd8a","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1975},"end":{"line":1986},"content_hash":"3661554d9ec3b6ade08fbb453c62e14c05eacd1871b109bac087e43dd7492399"},"suggested_fix":"Record invite.revoke (by expiry, actor system:expiry) for each invite the sweep finds lapsed, and person.rights {person, rights: null} for each row release_unconnected changes; add both to section 6.13.","summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"92eb68c6c559ff8100c7ff88faf9a9b9716b133ad410c3d630689dcff97d5883","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T15:50:05.979445Z","id":"63cb4ceee8070bb7ca207c0e3a295f4f748b3a05d00992033aa59925b306cc98","body":{"detail":"At 8446429: upsert_viewer(lan, 'Аlex') with no owner name succeeds; set_owner_name('Alex') then succeeds too, and both names stand. An agent registering from repository web is named 'web' beside a LAN viewer 'wеb'. New people are covered (check_person_name refuses a look-alike held by an uninvited viewer). The owner usually names themselves late, on a first comment, so pre-squatting is the likely order.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"d5b22f70e442ee22c3d2c8cecd9fb469a2ebea4e76d3e6523fb7899692b93d12"},"suggested_fix":"Mark it where names are shown: an unconnected viewer whose name looks like a protected name is flagged in the shell and in agent author lines (with spec section 9.6's '(not connected)', Task 17), rather than refusing the owner their own name.","summary":"The look-alike check runs only when the later name is set: a LAN viewer who took 'Аlex' before the owner named themselves 'Alex', or 'wеb' before an agent web went live, keeps it","supersedes":"2c3182731c84d005ef66708718194afec212d5003d1576e31cd87e7a6c985bcd","tags":["review","spec:9.6","revisit:task-17","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:00.376750Z","id":"ffb7d47d2d2cf5abd91269c96d06ba4605c220b73c4f2417090fa2d4ffe5244e","body":{"detail":"M17 lists rights, narrowing and elevation changes among the bump sources. Every source with a store write today calls Store::visibility_changed and is pinned by store::approvals::tests::every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once. The per-agent narrow and elevate routes arrive later; each, and any new write that sets viewers.person or person_revoked_at, must mark the change too, or the owner's fast path (Store::owner_sees_all, cached per generation) and rights caches go stale.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":259},"end":{"line":267},"content_hash":"c28dd7bfcd2dbdb2d9681cc69bc620ba9b5058d3016a9616178a80c1c35b54a2"},"suggested_fix":"Call self.visibility_changed() in the store methods that write sessions.narrow_json and elevate_json, and add them to every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once.","summary":"Agent narrowing and elevation do not bump the visibility generation yet: no write of sessions.narrow_json or elevate_json exists","supersedes":"69843dde6d973a5720977e84521e222f75d87c2089e76fd10557ee755d4712db","tags":["visibility","revisit:when agent narrowing and elevation are stored","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:00.377033Z","id":"3c67161a50aead1d19edb8b62856ac1ad3b6d95c2de34f095033d55ca52f27a8","body":{"detail":"record_tool_call selects audit_events by call_id alone. Since ea4daf0 a grant's x-clax-call counts, so a call_id sent by an agent of another machine joins an owner agent's tool.call (its produced list and the artifact the call belongs to) if the IDs collide. Call IDs are agent-minted ULIDs, so a collision needs a guessed or leaked ID; the risk is low, but the call index now spans credentials.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":453},"end":{"line":460},"content_hash":"fe045ef41d3509d21b9747bf185f6947ff224dd134b75f9b68571e5644ef801e"},"suggested_fix":"Filter produced by the reporting session (session_id = the report's session; NULL session and the same actor for the sessionless /api/tool-calls).","summary":"tool.call's produced list joins every event with the call_id, whoever recorded it","supersedes":"5819144b476b3e759440c7c18ed72d8ca312b9bc46c9f3248a53d12ed46cf472","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:00.377315Z","id":"d81624bf7825ae351e15bd3c9034aa004d6f48c4931e0d01efecc51e1ddb9d9a","body":{"detail":"For flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1086},"end":{"line":1100},"content_hash":"a055d17fb6d13921d9565129c8f0b702f534ab8d657151596b97465c24004831"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","supersedes":"79623e38cfcc9cd895a38f0b5b0f4429c5d515932313f4f5f1e18ccc4002694b","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:00.377568Z","id":"38f37a3de103e87434296c7d1b003eb90fb60a292f03948258f465252cd90286","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1997},"end":{"line":2008},"content_hash":"3661554d9ec3b6ade08fbb453c62e14c05eacd1871b109bac087e43dd7492399"},"suggested_fix":"Record invite.revoke (by expiry, actor system:expiry) for each invite the sweep finds lapsed, and person.rights {person, rights: null} for each row release_unconnected changes; add both to section 6.13.","summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"8e23afd215d98a3120cf8544db13284d7cde1b79ca73fc49e8c1c9d01a17fd8a","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.886817Z","id":"dd8c10380a6a3323acbfcb63222d10a7162d3ac6320474ba7918b98e99bc3a1e","body":{"detail":"M17 lists rights, narrowing and elevation changes among the bump sources. Every source with a store write today calls Store::visibility_changed and is pinned by store::approvals::tests::every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once. The per-agent narrow and elevate routes arrive later; each, and any new write that sets viewers.person or person_revoked_at, must mark the change too, or the owner's fast path (Store::owner_sees_all, cached per generation) and rights caches go stale.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":260},"end":{"line":268},"content_hash":"c28dd7bfcd2dbdb2d9681cc69bc620ba9b5058d3016a9616178a80c1c35b54a2"},"suggested_fix":"Call self.visibility_changed() in the store methods that write sessions.narrow_json and elevate_json, and add them to every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once.","summary":"Agent narrowing and elevation do not bump the visibility generation yet: no write of sessions.narrow_json or elevate_json exists","supersedes":"ffb7d47d2d2cf5abd91269c96d06ba4605c220b73c4f2417090fa2d4ffe5244e","tags":["visibility","revisit:when agent narrowing and elevation are stored","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.888938Z","id":"451f70a987cd46884830dee70a06413cb0e2ca14b93ca3f77e6ac78fd32cc36d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:45d8d5a","summary":"record_tool_call lists, and checks for an earlier tool.call among, only the events of the reporting agent's session (or the token's sessionless agent). Test: store::audit::tests::tool_call_lists_only_what_its_reporting_agent_produced passes.","supersedes":"3c67161a50aead1d19edb8b62856ac1ad3b6d95c2de34f095033d55ca52f27a8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T21:18:23.621071Z","id":"f1f3cb8d43728d2e8b88b05954a5c8f9c547e8eebebe72d85a3574ef439252c6","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam's agent posts POST /api/artifacts/{aid}/threads with anchor.file set to a guessed name on Mia's version: 400 invalid_anchor 'has no file' when it is absent, 201 (a new thread) when present. File names are withheld from Sam (spec §8.3 Version; GET …/files leaves them out once Task 10 filters it), so this is an existence oracle on them, at the cost of a visible thread per hit. The anchor's file must be one the reader may see before it is used.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":585},"end":{"line":594},"content_hash":"c9e89dabf916df39046475b503b2db3fcb2a9bda023016d9bfe852820e0ebfd0"},"suggested_fix":"For a person's agent, refuse an anchor on a file whose authors the reader may not see with the same answer as an absent file (or 403 withheld), checked before the thread is written.","summary":"Creating a thread tells a person's agent whether a version holds a file it may not see","tags":["review","visibility","depends:task-10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:14:39.268071Z","id":"c5c9ac210744ccd1ce724a94e02897361c0785bf3604472d5b3a586477f347cf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dbb6943","summary":"Fixed: thread creation takes the files the creator may not see as absent (Store::create_thread_hiding, crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs:532 and :621, fed by Vis::filter_anchor_file in routes/threads.rs create), after every check that comes before the file check, so a guessed name gets the same 400 invalid_anchor message as a missing one; index.html, which every version has, is never refused. Evidence: api_visibility::creating_a_thread_never_tells_whether_a_withheld_file_exists passes (Mia's FILE_NAME, CARRIED_NAME and a missing name answer identically, no thread written); dropping the hidden check fails it.","supersedes":"f1f3cb8d43728d2e8b88b05954a5c8f9c547e8eebebe72d85a3574ef439252c6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T23:45:17.865507Z","id":"86b11c7beacc7152301c969f94a21f1d5f97af92acae224c6d7c3870d9e24918","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam's agent (clax-db write) on an artifact holding N documents, k of them Mia's and withheld, creates documents until a create answers 400 quota_exceeded: the number it created is 5000 - N, so it learns N, including documents in collections it never names. withheld_count (spec §8.3) already discloses each collection's withheld count; this adds the total across collections. Every probe is a visible write credited to Sam's person, and Sam can delete them after. Spec §8.3 and §7.5 say nothing about the quota. At the quota a set on a named path also succeeds when it holds a document and fails when it does not, which the placeholder of GET on that path already discloses.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":625},"end":{"line":639},"content_hash":"c643520800cad49d67d4d6af759e1056606f8d33cf97ca0573c54a02951d5d14"},"suggested_fix":"Decide whether the total is acceptable (as withheld_count per collection is), or count the quota per author set (a reader's own and approved documents against a share of MAX_DOCS) and say so in §8.3.","summary":"The 5000-document quota counts documents an agent's person may not see, so filling the artifact up to it tells how many withheld documents it holds","tags":["people","spec:8.3","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T23:45:17.865611Z","id":"046c893784edc8ec4341ce294abe3f22cbacbc1294d192e00401c704e5c58dbd","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam's agent sends PATCH …/docs/notes/x with lww and one field of n bytes to Mia's withheld document; update_body merges it into her data and Body::new answers 400 invalid_argument (\"a document is at most 262144 bytes as JSON\") when her body plus n passes MAX_DOC_BYTES, else 200 with the placeholder. A failed probe writes nothing, so descending n until one succeeds learns her body's size to a byte at the cost of one visible write credited to Sam (which adds him to its authors). Spec §7.5 keeps blind PATCH allowed, and §8.3's placeholder holds no size; Task 10 withheld an asset's size for the same reason (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs filter_assets). PUT replaces the body and does not depend on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":791},"end":{"line":795},"content_hash":"2e791a3316a0f0b02e33f921317c3d9e440c413c865f3c9d501c71d36fdac2ed"},"suggested_fix":"Decide between (a) accepting it as a §21.7 limitation (each probe is a visible write credited to the prober's person; it gives a size, never content), and (b) treating an update as content-dependent on a withheld document (403 withheld before the merge, as str_replace), which leaves PUT, DELETE and batch set and delete blind but changes §7.5, which today keeps blind PATCH allowed.","summary":"A blind update (PATCH, batch update, acquire with data) on a withheld document fails when the merged body passes 256 KiB, which tells the document's size","tags":["people","spec:8.3","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T00:51:56.797987Z","id":"fd68a4aad55def97bf4d1657c13279637ac3d665aa16c41ee767bf8601f1cd25","body":{"detail":"Evidence (scratch probes on 8786478, crates/clax-server/tests/review_t11_probes.rs, not committed): Mia's agent PUTs notes/t {flag: true, text: hello} and notes/f {flag: false, text: hello}. Sam's agent sends the identical PATCH {data: {pad: 'a' x (262144 - len({flag:true,text:hello,pad:''}))}, lww: true} to both: notes/t answers 200 (written), notes/f answers 400 invalid_argument and keeps its version. So one request tells a withheld boolean, and the 'false' answer writes nothing. With a delete marker ({secret: {__delete__: true}, pad: ...}) the same request answers 200 where the field 'secret' exists and 400 where it does not, so a guessed field's presence is told too; descending pads tell a field's serialised length and whether it is an object (merge_into, crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs:417-435, merges objects and replaces anything else). The same holds for batch update (docs.rs update_body at :1212) and acquire with data (:1304). Spec §21.3 says content-dependent writes on withheld documents are refused; §7.5 lists blind PATCH as allowed; the two conflict for merges. Recommendation: treat a merge on a document withheld from the caller as content-dependent: PATCH, batch update and acquire with data answer 403 withheld with its withheld authors before the pin or the merge, exactly as str_replace (doc_str_replace_visible, :950-977); PUT, DELETE, batch set and delete, and acquire without data stay blind and allowed; amend the §7.5 docs row and §21.3 to say so. Accepting it under §21.7 instead would mean stating that a blind update tells a withheld document's field presence, types, lengths and boolean values.","kind":"comment","references":"046c893784edc8ec4341ce294abe3f22cbacbc1294d192e00401c704e5c58dbd","span":{"start":{"line":791},"end":{"line":795},"content_hash":"0fbc318f5c5b5890b5c942d56649991a76ee9076e0b93b9b775ec9d5aa78d431"},"summary":"The oracle tells field values and field presence, not only size, and its informative answer can be the failure that writes nothing","tags":["people","spec:7.5","spec:21.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T00:51:56.798158Z","id":"b475ca348392bf4f7d67c1ab5d1cbbcd5c5999cc8a661cc71111352ecdf73c9e","body":{"detail":"The quota tells a count, never a path or a value, and only after 5000 - N creations each credited to the prober's person (visible to the owner and to anyone who lists the collection); withheld_count (spec §8.3) already tells the per-collection count, so this adds the artifact-wide total and the documents in collections or rules-hidden subtrees the caller cannot name. Two neighbours tell the same kind of thing and should be named with it: MAX_LEASES (docs.rs:1278-1291) counts every lease in force, so acquiring until resource_exhausted tells how many leases others hold; and versions come from one artifact-wide sequence (next_version, docs.rs:531-538), so the gap between two of a caller's own write versions counts every write in between, withheld and rules-hidden documents included. A per-person quota would change single-owner behaviour and let an artifact hold 5000 documents per person. Suggested §21.7 sentence: 'an artifact's document and lease caps count every document and lease, and document versions come from one sequence per artifact, so an agent can count others' documents, leases and writes, never read them'.","kind":"comment","references":"86b11c7beacc7152301c969f94a21f1d5f97af92acae224c6d7c3870d9e24918","span":{"start":{"line":625},"end":{"line":639},"content_hash":"c643520800cad49d67d4d6af759e1056606f8d33cf97ca0573c54a02951d5d14"},"summary":"Recommend accepting the quota count as a documented limitation, with the lease cap and the version sequence beside it","tags":["people","spec:21.7","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T00:52:04.102320Z","id":"9103567780657aa801d05b366077902df96c27d321bab13fde9c7b380c66ce9d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5f5c275","summary":"Fixed as the coordinator ruled (refuse): PATCH, a batch update and acquire with data on a document withheld from the caller answer 403 withheld with its withheld authors before the pin or the merge (refuse_withheld in crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs; routes/docs.rs refusal); PUT, DELETE, batch set and delete and acquire without data stay blind; spec §7.5 docs row and §21.3 say so. Evidence: api_visibility::a_merge_never_tells_what_a_withheld_document_holds sends the review's pad PATCH, the delete-marker PATCH, a batch update and an acquire with data to {flag: true} and {flag: false}: identical 403 answers, nothing written; store::docs::tests::per_reader::a_merge_on_a_withheld_document_is_refused_before_it_is_evaluated. Mutation (update no longer refused) fails both and patch_returns_filtered_documents.","supersedes":"046c893784edc8ec4341ce294abe3f22cbacbc1294d192e00401c704e5c58dbd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T00:52:04.162578Z","id":"a5fc1839d10cd22d9aaa56a5f9f223ee140894b046d2715acf2adda5bb8a3fcf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5f5c275","summary":"Decided by the coordinator: accepted as a count disclosure. Spec §21.7 now names it: an artifact's document and lease caps (5000 documents, 100 leases in force) count every document and lease, and document versions come from one sequence per artifact, so an agent can count others' documents, leases and writes, never read them. No code change.","supersedes":"86b11c7beacc7152301c969f94a21f1d5f97af92acae224c6d7c3870d9e24918","tags":["status:decided","reason:wontfix","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.787444Z","id":"bd89b6edcb1badbfa832c314271b2743eed8cea46168e92e9dc4126be7d6bbda","body":{"detail":"status:decided means a human (the owner) made the call (qualifier conventions). The close a5fc1839 records the coordinator's ruling that accepts the quota count as a count disclosure named in spec §21.7. Read it as the coordinator's decision, which the owner may still revisit.","kind":"comment","references":"a5fc1839d10cd22d9aaa56a5f9f223ee140894b046d2715acf2adda5bb8a3fcf","summary":"Attribution: the coordinator made this ruling and the owner was informed; the owner did not make the call, so the status:decided tag on the close above is wrong","tags":["people","spec:21.7","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.790325Z","id":"d784c2d56cc6616e5452ff0ba324325a5191f176610ebd6f3b6eca9d1f7f1719","body":{"detail":"reset_placeholders runs on every approval made (any_author false) and revoked (any_author true). A made approval clears placeholder_at on undelivered rows of the approver's sessions in its scope whose comment the approved author wrote, or that a page wrote (via_page: page authors are not matched), or on every row when it approves *unconnected. A row whose body another author still withholds (a page-written comment, or the *unconnected class) is held again at the next take and its session gets a second placeholder line for it. Clearing on approval is what makes feedback_state read sent rather than withheld for rows the approval lets through (state_of reads placeholder_at). Matching each row's full author set here would need the visibility filter inside the approval's transaction.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"cfba753a774613eb13d8d57051d1f477a5412f4ad3882badfd8eae541e270bee"},"summary":"An approval clears placeholder_at by its author's comments in scope, so a page-written row, or one also withheld for another author, is told once more after it","tags":["people","spec:8.4","spec:9.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.791541Z","id":"9b973953c887d5984b464bd9683dc0401a0415b823fa125a8a6c1e9ca1336cc4","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (with the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds a row and tells the session. A comment sent to an idle agent whose person has not approved its author reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take (piggyback, a hook, a wait). Computing it at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which thread listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1466},"end":{"line":1480},"content_hash":"cf1feeb1f08b4f16222b5a1971c305f899e006bf11ef1bedd1029335750f48da"},"summary":"feedback_state reads withheld only once a take has held the row; until then a held row reads sent","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:55.164400Z","id":"a8976ac7b8c07a1d28af0a8980dc5f4ee26125e1c166053c220aaed962c71e7e","body":{"detail":"M17 lists rights, narrowing and elevation changes among the bump sources. Every source with a store write today calls Store::visibility_changed and is pinned by store::approvals::tests::every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once. The per-agent narrow and elevate routes arrive later; each, and any new write that sets viewers.person or person_revoked_at, must mark the change too, or the owner's fast path (Store::owner_sees_all, cached per generation) and rights caches go stale.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":322},"end":{"line":330},"content_hash":"c28dd7bfcd2dbdb2d9681cc69bc620ba9b5058d3016a9616178a80c1c35b54a2"},"suggested_fix":"Call self.visibility_changed() in the store methods that write sessions.narrow_json and elevate_json, and add them to every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once.","summary":"Agent narrowing and elevation do not bump the visibility generation yet: no write of sessions.narrow_json or elevate_json exists","supersedes":"dd8c10380a6a3323acbfcb63222d10a7162d3ac6320474ba7918b98e99bc3a1e","tags":["visibility","revisit:when agent narrowing and elevation are stored","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:55.165627Z","id":"1542550d6421985e56c877306ea05a05b5730b90644a969f7d9ca75f97613205","body":{"detail":"send_in skips every viewer comment that has a feedback row for any target, so POST …/threads/<tid>/send {to} after the thread went to another agent inserts no rows for the new one, though it becomes the thread's target. Store::send_to_named (used for @name) instead checks rows per target, so the two ways of sending to one agent differ.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":183},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"4d26296fbd266f8c3776482cc19d813aa85b511f7becea3cb9a44c98292d4c92"},"suggested_fix":"Decide whether a send with to should, like @name, give the named agent every comment it has no row for (spec §12 makes it the thread's owner).","summary":"A send with to on a thread whose comments already have rows gives the named agent nothing","supersedes":"92e4398f5b69223950271250988c91747dfa19ede18d380b3589510945ab8e70","tags":["spec:12","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T03:47:26.797446Z","id":"18aabaa0a8e472562b5f4260eefa39d73ed9f2f4701a7ae3dc729067575806dd","body":{"detail":"reset_placeholders runs on every approval made and revoked. It clears placeholder_at on undelivered rows of the approver's sessions in its scope whose comment the approval's author wrote, or that a page wrote (via_page: page authors are not matched), or on every row when it is of *unconnected. A page-written row, or one whose body another author also withholds, is held again at the next take after such an approval or revocation, and its session gets a second placeholder line for it. Clearing on approval is what makes feedback_state read sent rather than withheld for rows the approval lets through (state_of reads placeholder_at). Matching each row's full author set here would need the visibility filter inside the approval's transaction.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":195},"content_hash":"60c9708b441dc12ea94e920acd0ae2e18dabac75aaeca11bf34663ccb1cb9078"},"summary":"An approval clears placeholder_at by its author's comments in scope, so a page-written row, or one also withheld for another author, is told once more after it","supersedes":"d784c2d56cc6616e5452ff0ba324325a5191f176610ebd6f3b6eca9d1f7f1719","tags":["people","spec:8.4","spec:9.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T03:47:26.797887Z","id":"e9efa496071c8b573be0d13ba1f841c38df599c458d16ef76b873eb658f127a7","body":{"detail":"M17 lists rights, narrowing and elevation changes among the bump sources. Every source with a store write today calls Store::visibility_changed and is pinned by store::approvals::tests::every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once. The per-agent narrow and elevate routes arrive later; each, and any new write that sets viewers.person or person_revoked_at, must mark the change too, or the owner's fast path (Store::owner_sees_all, cached per generation) and rights caches go stale.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":318},"end":{"line":326},"content_hash":"c28dd7bfcd2dbdb2d9681cc69bc620ba9b5058d3016a9616178a80c1c35b54a2"},"suggested_fix":"Call self.visibility_changed() in the store methods that write sessions.narrow_json and elevate_json, and add them to every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once.","summary":"Agent narrowing and elevation do not bump the visibility generation yet: no write of sessions.narrow_json or elevate_json exists","supersedes":"a8976ac7b8c07a1d28af0a8980dc5f4ee26125e1c166053c220aaed962c71e7e","tags":["visibility","revisit:when agent narrowing and elevation are stored","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T03:47:26.799518Z","id":"9a2c3d8cf54daf31b3eff6dfcbf380b6919fa28ba8349514697dc6e04aa656d0","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (with the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds a row and tells the session. A comment sent to an idle agent whose person has not approved its author reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take (piggyback, a hook, a wait). Computing it at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which thread listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1527},"end":{"line":1541},"content_hash":"cf1feeb1f08b4f16222b5a1971c305f899e006bf11ef1bedd1029335750f48da"},"summary":"feedback_state reads withheld only once a take has held the row; until then a held row reads sent","supersedes":"9b973953c887d5984b464bd9683dc0401a0415b823fa125a8a6c1e9ca1336cc4","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T05:42:22.074457Z","id":"f65565e2246c4c4f70c505215a200f7a8026f3e0c1f40762ec870cc6eb7bdc74","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2011},"end":{"line":2022},"content_hash":"3661554d9ec3b6ade08fbb453c62e14c05eacd1871b109bac087e43dd7492399"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"38f37a3de103e87434296c7d1b003eb90fb60a292f03948258f465252cd90286","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T05:42:22.077002Z","id":"e49e3c53a3ddadd15d17cf6a20f5b44b0107025a9c5d4142e9bebb3a6e31721c","body":{"detail":"connection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1201},"end":{"line":1206},"content_hash":"37faa7c25489c7bb21c58449a00b215ba4670c56c30156fd84acd0324fb5acb1"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T05:42:22.077149Z","id":"acd2b0ce727d39b6e58f7250722c85103694895e7bd62f2ad4e35276a7247884","body":{"detail":"note_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1390},"end":{"line":1394},"content_hash":"a0fa4a8c2b1a39edfb532ddd9c70fe377bd2d0458f5500bbff31400339dff010"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T06:46:08.079496Z","id":"9faaa3589a643aa6554297355fee029411fa1b7f6868e33b55b19998f25b518c","body":{"detail":"Failure: a home at migration 25 where a person's agent asked a question (a dev home run on this branch) keeps that question's item with recipient NULL after 26, so it sits in the owner's inbox and crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs render reads its question unscoped (st.question), showing the person's question and answers to the owner, while the person never gets the item. Main's homes hold no person sessions, so they are unaffected. Accepted: migrations 24-26 are unmerged (spec M27), so only a dev home run on this branch can hold such items; questions themselves get their person from their session (questions.person is filled in by the migration).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":706},"end":{"line":709},"content_hash":"4611fbab17797ab78415d9f71e991c5b174e8ca88f75ff87d6685c7d8474fc79"},"summary":"Migration 26 leaves every existing inbox item the owner's, including question and finished items a connected person's agent made at schema 24-25","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T06:48:40.551885Z","id":"0a32894e3fc0867b8de5d28c3ae7bb745138af86122f0b654321c01f9f4f7fe6","body":{"detail":"connection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1219},"end":{"line":1224},"content_hash":"37faa7c25489c7bb21c58449a00b215ba4670c56c30156fd84acd0324fb5acb1"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","supersedes":"e49e3c53a3ddadd15d17cf6a20f5b44b0107025a9c5d4142e9bebb3a6e31721c","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T06:48:40.552347Z","id":"d756b91978499edd0968319a248bd459958ba8c8e68128689296db2c84b4fcc5","body":{"detail":"note_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1408},"end":{"line":1412},"content_hash":"a0fa4a8c2b1a39edfb532ddd9c70fe377bd2d0458f5500bbff31400339dff010"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","supersedes":"acd2b0ce727d39b6e58f7250722c85103694895e7bd62f2ad4e35276a7247884","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.108074Z","id":"d9fb0be608fcfff98d859883ebcfdddf71178581b63a4b7a356bfbf6b1237306","body":{"detail":"M17 lists rights, narrowing and elevation changes among the bump sources. Every source with a store write today calls Store::visibility_changed and is pinned by store::approvals::tests::every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once. The per-agent narrow and elevate routes arrive later; each, and any new write that sets viewers.person or person_revoked_at, must mark the change too, or the owner's fast path (Store::owner_sees_all, cached per generation) and rights caches go stale.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":365},"end":{"line":373},"content_hash":"c28dd7bfcd2dbdb2d9681cc69bc620ba9b5058d3016a9616178a80c1c35b54a2"},"suggested_fix":"Call self.visibility_changed() in the store methods that write sessions.narrow_json and elevate_json, and add them to every_visibility_change_bumps_the_generation_once.","summary":"Agent narrowing and elevation do not bump the visibility generation yet: no write of sessions.narrow_json or elevate_json exists","supersedes":"e9efa496071c8b573be0d13ba1f841c38df599c458d16ef76b873eb658f127a7","tags":["visibility","revisit:when agent narrowing and elevation are stored","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.108620Z","id":"8a296aab4c5f337a8baa71e579c86e4effdc68efee4e1f7f666eaa14c81b7d91","body":{"detail":"connection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1277},"end":{"line":1282},"content_hash":"37faa7c25489c7bb21c58449a00b215ba4670c56c30156fd84acd0324fb5acb1"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","supersedes":"0a32894e3fc0867b8de5d28c3ae7bb745138af86122f0b654321c01f9f4f7fe6","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.109046Z","id":"b5db7a3a18966129939f1c920338dc94289b1dbbb3e4873d11df8d601d2da56f","body":{"detail":"note_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1466},"end":{"line":1470},"content_hash":"a0fa4a8c2b1a39edfb532ddd9c70fe377bd2d0458f5500bbff31400339dff010"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","supersedes":"d756b91978499edd0968319a248bd459958ba8c8e68128689296db2c84b4fcc5","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.109495Z","id":"4377760ee0b2eaa95a21d4cb5f9fad326c6ff7186bbbd6a03585dee233c3b9dc","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2012},"end":{"line":2023},"content_hash":"3661554d9ec3b6ade08fbb453c62e14c05eacd1871b109bac087e43dd7492399"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"f65565e2246c4c4f70c505215a200f7a8026f3e0c1f40762ec870cc6eb7bdc74","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.113283Z","id":"da8b82c56ceacf3cdcd02d0f1f2df4887d6a3010034ab72ebb24b841a31c49a6","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a routed send, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a later reply on a sent thread whose author has no open request, or an author an approver is full for) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1608},"end":{"line":1617},"content_hash":"a3dbcea7dba65243e385e59851ada6e94fd7769e8e4e38ca58cf6b66c227091d"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"9a2c3d8cf54daf31b3eff6dfcbf380b6919fa28ba8349514697dc6e04aa656d0","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.114982Z","id":"43316c1b0ff1531454fd6ba95dce2363719de3d688e76f6ed1203fc92f17d5be","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7cda419","summary":"release_told clears placeholder_at only on rows whose body every author lets through, judged by a Visibility built on the approval's transaction (Visibility::for_reader_in), and revocation clears nothing: store::approvals::tests::an_approval_releases_exactly_the_rows_it_lets_through and a_revoked_approval_tells_its_rows_once_more pass; the first fails when the seen check is removed.","supersedes":"18aabaa0a8e472562b5f4260eefa39d73ed9f2f4701a7ae3dc729067575806dd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.115299Z","id":"5a2f9341ffcdaaa9e62bf161fffb26694d51ff400d6fce1378fd9501dc7120e2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7cda419","summary":"send_in now gives a send to one agent every viewer comment it has no row for, its untargeted rows first, as send_to_named does: store::feedback::tests::a_send_to_one_agent_is_followed_by_later_comments_until_it_ends asserts the named agent gets first, second, third and fourth.","supersedes":"1542550d6421985e56c877306ea05a05b5730b90644a969f7d9ca75f97613205","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.115698Z","id":"069869bf67e9ac3c721723849e8c7cb6fe594c333c3ec0fcfdfbe69a55014897","body":{"detail":"request_in sets the install row approval_overflow:<approver> when routing finds the approver holding MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) open requests and holds the content without one (spec §9.2). Only Store::decide_request clears it, once fewer than 100 are open. Requests withdrawn by a resolve, delete, session end or person revocation lower the count without clearing it, so GET /api/approvals/requests keeps returning the banner until the approver decides something. Content held without a request stays held either way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1001},"end":{"line":1007},"content_hash":"470c155279fca671dab9583940923b782429698e53fec685411548db3c315f90"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.115780Z","id":"e94d02686c21c207cd77bfa4035dc31b6e544f61394586ea3545b2d15f3e9b0f","body":{"detail":"withheld_in_thread counts the authors withheld from each comment body (the rows a take holds, spec M16). A thread whose comments the agent may see but whose anchor, clip or artifact title is another person's (spec §3.3 step 6) is delivered with those fields placeholdered and makes no request; the agent can ask for the artifact's content outside threads with ask {approval: {url_or_id}} (Store::ask_approval, withheld_outside_threads), which covers text fields, the current version, documents and assets, but not a thread's anchor.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1147},"end":{"line":1167},"content_hash":"2db7bc0ea49daabf8d49defd3d54488b8041d0c22a95068bc6531cfc23d68cee"},"summary":"Routing asks only for the authors of comment bodies; a withheld anchor, clip, batch note or title makes no request","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.115855Z","id":"af10c3c92eb9b0bde02f491ef6c06e46cea000b7ad4e205daac6feb540d1070d","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.3: 'Declining keeps the rows held; a later ask there makes a new request only after 10 minutes'. request_in applies the same quiet period to routing, so a sender pressing Send again right after the approver declined does not re-announce the request; the rows are held and the agent's placeholder reads as not asked. If the owner wants a deliberate re-send to ask at once, drop the check for Cause::Routing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":984},"end":{"line":993},"content_hash":"cf9707d61e55687d29484ea3ec1da7a8faa513bbca583c591bf81438ce7a4e23"},"summary":"A routed send within ten minutes of a decline makes no request, though spec §9.3 names only ask","tags":["people","spec:9.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T08:26:18.115972Z","id":"8579ddc427cd90216114610a3a4070f37171421cf7e9ca8868ce5812bd4b6cb1","body":{"detail":"route_in runs for every session a send reaches (send_in's targets): a send without `to` reaches every live owner and watcher of the artifact, so each of their people who has not approved the thread's authors is asked (spec M18: a send 'that reaches an agent'). Spec §9.2 says 'targets an agent'; read narrowly, only `to`, @name, handoff and a page's send would ask. In the two-person canary world Mia's untargeted batch now puts a request in the owner's inbox.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1178},"end":{"line":1186},"content_hash":"4e424858f75b0edad5559cc291778e645b3cdb9d249e118bf2d5667550ec213b"},"summary":"An untargeted send asks the person of every agent it reaches, the owner included","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:05:16.919133Z","id":"fc6e57be3d940bfc73052c7e3221e68505137e580ad348358e7257adf1d2900b","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam's browser starts 100 threads on an artifact the owner's agent watches and presses Send on each (no `to`); each makes an open request to the owner (route_in, request_in), the owner's inbox shows 100 unread approval cards, and GET /api/approvals/requests shows the overflow banner. Mia's next send `to` the owner's agent then finds `held >= MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS` here and is held without a request. Shown by a scratch probe against 2f10f67 (owner open=100, Mia's thread has no request). The count is per approver only (spec §9.2); nothing bounds one author's share, the same shape as the global question cap fixed in Task 13.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1099},"end":{"line":1116},"content_hash":"4e30c09418df5b33634cdee16897f7e70a6bcaef9cedf89e9486756bc0d1db72"},"suggested_fix":"Bound each (approver, author) pair as well, for example at most 20 open requests per author for one approver with the 100 per approver kept: past an author's share, join that author's newest open request for the approver (raise its count) instead of holding without a request. Amend spec §9.2 with the rule and test that one author's flood leaves another author's first send a request.","summary":"One author can fill an approver's 100 open requests, so routed content from everyone else reaches that approver with no request","tags":["review","people","spec:9.2","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:05:16.919269Z","id":"1bbfd23f9f9417d783ea252084143f42c2cab920a7ea253a9f56218d513dba7c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8579ddc427cd90216114610a3a4070f37171421cf7e9ca8868ce5812bd4b6cb1","summary":"Measured against 2f10f67: the owner pressing Send without `to` on their own thread, after Mia replied there, put a request in Sam's inbox because Sam's agent watches the page. Every person with a watching agent gets a card for each such thread the owner sends to their own agents. Reading untargeted sends as joins (open requests only, with the placeholder telling the agent how to ask) would remove that noise.","tags":["review","people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:06:02.242593Z","id":"5b39eb1780f69338df31eeff26c661fe56d86b76ff694ad83d9ca09f93d49a07","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1621},"end":{"line":1630},"content_hash":"58070c3dc3bfd0816571f2b422f4f5498db2d6bcc2400ea7e8d12f9c3497b53f"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"da8b82c56ceacf3cdcd02d0f1f2df4887d6a3010034ab72ebb24b841a31c49a6","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:06:02.243199Z","id":"7e85ea5b5c1af50ce1023ee6c16525dcf28183d5d67de3373519b7ef820f9d35","body":{"detail":"The overflow marker (install row approval_overflow:<approver>) lists the [author, artifact, thread] places whose routed content request_in held without a request, past MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) per approver or MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR (20) per author. Only Store::decide_request rechecks them, dropping a place once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request: answered by an open or declined request, delivered, gone, or now visible). A withdrawal or an approval made outside a decision changes nothing until the next decision, so the banner can outlive what it counted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1843},"end":{"line":1853},"content_hash":"73f004277ac55d0d5d175ac9d9633a7b394f8ae4a809ba5e85e370048b9398ee"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","supersedes":"069869bf67e9ac3c721723849e8c7cb6fe594c333c3ec0fcfdfbe69a55014897","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:06:02.243679Z","id":"d464a0943a57bf6a2f5f62391091b20241462ab70ef0b3994e99bb08c1051b74","body":{"detail":"withheld_in_thread counts the authors withheld from each comment body (the rows a take holds, spec M16). A thread whose comments the agent may see but whose anchor, clip or artifact title is another person's (spec §3.3 step 6) is delivered with those fields placeholdered and makes no request; the agent can ask for the artifact's content outside threads with ask {approval: {url_or_id}} (Store::ask_approval, withheld_outside_threads), which covers text fields, the current version, documents and assets, but not a thread's anchor.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1256},"end":{"line":1276},"content_hash":"2db7bc0ea49daabf8d49defd3d54488b8041d0c22a95068bc6531cfc23d68cee"},"summary":"Routing asks only for the authors of comment bodies; a withheld anchor, clip, batch note or title makes no request","supersedes":"e94d02686c21c207cd77bfa4035dc31b6e544f61394586ea3545b2d15f3e9b0f","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:06:02.244129Z","id":"a8e309e03984dc79e2fc898101fc66493599b0e0de4c628ff1c533559aa12189","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.3: 'Declining keeps the rows held; a later ask there makes a new request only after 10 minutes'. request_in applies the same quiet period to routing, so a sender pressing Send again right after the approver declined does not re-announce the request; the rows are held and the agent's placeholder reads as not asked. If the owner wants a deliberate re-send to ask at once, drop the check for Cause::Routing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1082},"end":{"line":1091},"content_hash":"cf9707d61e55687d29484ea3ec1da7a8faa513bbca583c591bf81438ce7a4e23"},"summary":"A routed send within ten minutes of a decline makes no request, though spec §9.3 names only ask","supersedes":"af10c3c92eb9b0bde02f491ef6c06e46cea000b7ad4e205daac6feb540d1070d","tags":["people","spec:9.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:06:02.244895Z","id":"dcaf16cfa7dc7b9d73b6e0413841ec039511a5a98b47cb90ec535ff4eb8fe23b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e08870b","summary":"Ruled by the coordinator (not the owner): beside the 100 per approver, each (approver, author) holds at most MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR = 20 open requests; past it the author's further routed content is held silently with placeholders and joins People's banner (spec §9.2 amended). api_approvals::one_persons_sends_cannot_block_anothers_request (Sam's 100 sends to the owner's agent leave Mia's send a request) and store::approvals::tests::one_author_cannot_spend_an_approvers_requests pass; both fail with the per-author check removed.","supersedes":"fc6e57be3d940bfc73052c7e3221e68505137e580ad348358e7257adf1d2900b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:06:02.245617Z","id":"2ec76ee189389256871493004b6aee2cb9bf6a488319bc28a179ef18bf2c1a9d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e08870b","summary":"The owner decided (2026-10-11): \"Only named sends ask\". A send naming no agent asks no one (Store::send_routed reads it as Route::Join; a batch without `to` likewise); only a send naming an agent (the picker, `to`, `@name`, a batch or a page's sendToClaude naming one) makes a request. Spec M18 and §9.2 amended. api_approvals::a_send_naming_no_agent_asks_no_one and store::approvals::tests::only_a_send_naming_an_agent_asks pass.","supersedes":"8579ddc427cd90216114610a3a4070f37171421cf7e9ca8868ce5812bd4b6cb1","tags":["reason:fixed","status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:58:21.951466Z","id":"b9b20f8a9bc739486ce4f100f394298b7fb4a777cbb7f1a7578328cf14b21ccd","body":{"detail":"SendTarget::Agent moves threads.target_session_id to the named session but does not delete other sessions' undelivered rows, unlike the first take (take_in, crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs) and Store::handoff. The previous owner can still be handed those comments, and its reply is then refused with 409 thread_taken. Spec 2026-10-08 section 12 says people take over by sending again, without saying what happens to the old owner's pending rows.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":113},"end":{"line":125},"content_hash":"e007d78c080d706583dbb4242b58e555c3f4292389c58f7f23c123cd782d1196"},"summary":"A send naming a new agent leaves the previous owner's undelivered rows of the thread in place","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:58:21.951619Z","id":"765303748181cdf8339f71b4d52137fe0f0f561baa235583736550894afa4338","body":{"detail":"take_in deletes every other session's undelivered rows of the thread, held (withheld, placeholder_at set) rows included. When that session's person has an open request from ask for the thread, approving it later releases nothing to that agent, and the placeholder it was told of points at rows that are gone. Withdrawing such requests (approval.withdraw) or keeping held rows would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":266},"end":{"line":340},"content_hash":"eade51f59cdf39c269693e21d2a9bf4de21a60da2468df25017d3bb75e6ccb59"},"summary":"A first take deletes other sessions' held rows, leaving their open ask requests with nothing to release","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:58:21.951717Z","id":"df05efa6e1c32513c89b8c887c0437906b96b89aa8daf5149422acd2d29feea0","body":{"detail":"Ownership checks (check_not_taken_in, check_may_hand_off_in in crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs) treat an ended owner as no owner, so behaviour follows spec 2026-10-08 M23. But end_in neither clears the owner nor records thread.release with reason session_end or grant_revoked (spec section 20.2), and the ended note of section 14 cannot count released threads until it does.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1008},"end":{"line":1015},"content_hash":"d0b35d6a7c52d1544ca6e1b873530e4a3ac39b907e7f517065f2f2cec098f644"},"summary":"Ending a session leaves threads.target_session_id pointing at it and records no thread.release","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T14:58:41.794958Z","id":"ccd067bc680cc7009593bf514c4b9824f3e0d480d82b9d7e1a574e325780edb4","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1823},"end":{"line":1832},"content_hash":"58070c3dc3bfd0816571f2b422f4f5498db2d6bcc2400ea7e8d12f9c3497b53f"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"5b39eb1780f69338df31eeff26c661fe56d86b76ff694ad83d9ca09f93d49a07","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T16:47:38.360128Z","id":"b026f338e88573ca83778cc17fdfc5f46ca4112b78c4bffc1fde03dd2026501e","body":{"detail":"The overflow marker (install row approval_overflow:<approver>) lists the [author, artifact, thread] places whose routed content request_in held without a request, past MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) per approver or MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR (20) per author. Only Store::decide_request rechecks them, dropping a place once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request: answered by an open or declined request, delivered, gone, or now visible). A withdrawal or an approval made outside a decision changes nothing until the next decision, so the banner can outlive what it counted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1865},"end":{"line":1875},"content_hash":"73f004277ac55d0d5d175ac9d9633a7b394f8ae4a809ba5e85e370048b9398ee"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","supersedes":"7e85ea5b5c1af50ce1023ee6c16525dcf28183d5d67de3373519b7ef820f9d35","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T16:47:38.360746Z","id":"7f7f58a66148f64f1e0b9354d4762f1a01db5a01863102b890f7fa709a79604d","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1870},"end":{"line":1879},"content_hash":"58070c3dc3bfd0816571f2b422f4f5498db2d6bcc2400ea7e8d12f9c3497b53f"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"ccd067bc680cc7009593bf514c4b9824f3e0d480d82b9d7e1a574e325780edb4","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T16:47:38.362042Z","id":"02fde799398d1c588341d6ad81e63e47a20fbb8482b60bb0c7639b30a56a035b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1f0f12a","summary":"Fixed in 1f0f12a: an implicit take removes only the taker's own person's agents' rows (take_in), so other people's held rows and their asks stay; the rows it removes have their sessions' open ask requests withdrawn in the same transaction (approval.withdraw, reason thread_taken). Evidence: store::feedback::delivery::a_first_take_withdraws_the_asks_of_the_rows_it_removes and api_approvals::an_ask_still_delivers_after_another_persons_agent_takes pass.","supersedes":"765303748181cdf8339f71b4d52137fe0f0f561baa235583736550894afa4338","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T15:06:06.687599Z","id":"e33b9e77035f46b0445b371998eb9ecfbe98f3c24b4e4808f9fe2e001c8d9a4a","body":{"detail":"approve_owner_on_connect accepts any continuation call carrying {\"clax\": {\"approve_owner\": true}} on an issued grant (crates/clax-server/src/routes/grants.rs poll). remote.json holds the continuation token in the person's home, so a process of theirs with shell access (an agent included) can record the approval later. What it can record is only the person's approval of the owner's content, everywhere, created_via connect: the answer M15 makes the default, which the person revokes in People. The access token agents sign with cannot say it (crates/clax-server/tests/api_grants.rs a_connected_machine_approves_the_owner_through_its_continuation).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1474},"end":{"line":1535},"content_hash":"c38756f01d12705842fb15d611eaf61d31f30b78ff17f9a5adc0c0ab3e11749a"},"summary":"The person's approval of the owner can be recorded with the continuation token at any time, not only while clax connect runs","tags":["security","spec:6.3","M15","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T15:45:51.491783Z","id":"eb3fe53b5ebb95da0bd20d15a3fee0fb5479334999d96645e9da3f5a4bbf9166","body":{"detail":"approve_owner_on_connect is the single approval made without a browser (spec section 21 item 3, M15). It is bounded to the connect: once per grant, within OWNER_ANSWER_SECS (10 minutes) of the tokens' issue, never once the person has made or revoked any approval of the owner (409 owner_answered, so a revocation in People stands; 409 answer_closed after the window), replays refused by accept_t first. Only the continuation token says it, never the access token agents sign with (crates/clax-server/tests/api_grants.rs a_connected_machine_approves_the_owner_through_its_continuation), and clax connect refuses on an agent channel (crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs connect_refuses_on_an_agent_channel). What remains: a process of the person's that reads remote.json within those ten minutes, before clax connect answers, could answer yes for them; the person can revoke it in People, and that revocation is final. Tests: store::people::tests::connecting_records_the_persons_approval_of_the_owner_once, the_answer_about_the_owner_never_overrides_the_person.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1478},"end":{"line":1570},"content_hash":"d5ef04715b7251bf982fd51818c94f17a2b0b3b2dd3450f46854211db24ca24d"},"summary":"The person's approval of the owner is recorded without a browser once, at connect: an agent present then could answer for the person","supersedes":"e33b9e77035f46b0445b371998eb9ecfbe98f3c24b4e4808f9fe2e001c8d9a4a","tags":["security","spec:6.3","spec:21","M15","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T15:45:51.494679Z","id":"f9c8ae5247a5d12e7daf21e39eba8c58f4435b6dbc32b09960418576273645a3","body":{"detail":"For flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1089},"end":{"line":1103},"content_hash":"a055d17fb6d13921d9565129c8f0b702f534ab8d657151596b97465c24004831"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","supersedes":"d81624bf7825ae351e15bd3c9034aa004d6f48c4931e0d01efecc51e1ddb9d9a","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T15:45:51.495151Z","id":"f279547a08f03c884d9fb5356e98258bcf9059d31d99092b41a8077023532bf3","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2109},"end":{"line":2120},"content_hash":"3661554d9ec3b6ade08fbb453c62e14c05eacd1871b109bac087e43dd7492399"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"4377760ee0b2eaa95a21d4cb5f9fad326c6ff7186bbbd6a03585dee233c3b9dc","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:30.046965Z","id":"fd9200fba44cd845dc8a0c3acaf5c9b7206f2d706842b11243812729f8f7410a","body":{"detail":"release_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1369},"end":{"line":1385},"content_hash":"ed1cb058eed0b38a9d4e07ae6c733539b4ca4c1c6388d6f7a4614ccf4b5c1af2"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:30.047206Z","id":"81ecb6e033ed72a41b9c8a14571de14b351bf4136503663425030820420d37ff","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §6.7 fixes the note's text for an idle end; restore_note uses it for every idle end, but a local session (no grant_id) is reaped after Store::SESSION_IDLE_SECS (300 s) once its process is gone, and may re-register with the same harness session ID (a resumed harness session) and get the note.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1136},"end":{"line":1146},"content_hash":"33d6cc0ac2b9c830f69205737a38ded66546cec122d8bf18a39846ff67c1a342"},"suggested_fix":"Name the actual window, or restore local sessions' watches without the note.","summary":"The restore note says 30 minutes even when a local session ended after the 5-minute local window","tags":["spec:6.7","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:30.047302Z","id":"2bca898d378c76a8059d4e3f0009909a5868aef84d8f9ce8038c7ba8847b6c17","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §12 lets an agent of an ended owner's person hand off a thread with no live owner; §14 item 3 releases every thread at the end, so check_may_hand_off_in never sees an ended owner and only the implicit-take test (may_take_in) remains. A thread the owner sent to Sam's agent, once that agent ends, can no longer be handed off by Sam's other agents. Pinned by store::feedback::delivery::an_ended_owners_thread_is_handed_off_only_by_its_person_or_a_taker and ownership::owner_ended_threads_accept_any_agent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":287},"end":{"line":300},"content_hash":"07ca314f618b288ff0f2b8bd9862bac9994f26b68bbab87d65dc92669e5e9150"},"summary":"Since an end releases its threads, the ended-owner clause of the handoff rule never applies","tags":["spec:12","spec:14","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:30.047348Z","id":"be96345a6602ad567a26485a37e39dd25d4afc31049120f818225ae649eadb35","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b9b20f8a9bc739486ce4f100f394298b7fb4a777cbb7f1a7578328cf14b21ccd","summary":"Left open by the session-end cleanup (4f6952d): this is a send-time ownership rule, not an end-of-session effect. Fixing it needs a ruling on whether a send naming a new agent deletes only the previous owner's undelivered rows or, as a handoff does, every other session's (other people's agents included), and send_in has no store or audit context to withdraw the asks those rows hold (reason thread_taken).","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:30.047378Z","id":"b716a778a5f0b6382bd997aa9f43bbd11d22c36be0d6ca943bc1cda686ee88b6","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d9fb0be608fcfff98d859883ebcfdddf71178581b63a4b7a356bfbf6b1237306","summary":"Part done in 4f6952d: a session's end clears narrow_json and elevate_json and calls visibility_changed when either was set (Store::clear_rights_in in crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs, pinned by store::sessions::tests::cleanup::ending_a_session_cleans_up_and_leaves_one_note). The routes that set them still do not exist.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:30.047405Z","id":"aec2126d5c3eacab4f4b8c348a4131aec71203be38a1c7b70f71cd037aa794fe","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4f6952d","summary":"Fixed: end_in clears target_session_id of every thread the session owns and records thread.release (session_end, or grant_revoked for a revoked end); cargo test -p clax-core --lib sessions::tests::cleanup passes (ending_a_session_cleans_up_and_leaves_one_note, revoking_a_grant_ends_its_sessions_with_their_notes).","supersedes":"df05efa6e1c32513c89b8c887c0437906b96b89aa8daf5149422acd2d29feea0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.878321Z","id":"2d5730fd1be34f1dad49416c48f9edf2fe8d5dab89bd35d49dc013a21c620780","body":{"detail":"Registration derives a name from the repository and branch (spec section 11) without an event; session.start's body is harness, harness_session_id, cwd, transcript_path and pid. The first agent.name then reports previous: <derived name> with no earlier event naming it, and an @name in a comment cannot be tied to its session from the journal alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":173},"end":{"line":179},"content_hash":"2531645c1bbef5581474f3318cd70a2a599ab739af3be8223fbe8da994159a5b"},"suggested_fix":"Add name (classed as a name for redaction) to session.start and session.join bodies, and say so in audit spec section 6.8.","summary":"A session's derived name is never recorded, so agent.name's previous names a value the journal never held","supersedes":"a40cabad94e6b3b1c0cf1c0ff82e5a41cc4de0f9bc78a6e7cf891fcbaed965e9","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.879021Z","id":"0118687f2dc557d8b4b673cfea9e3a7e7911afa2f991c90dad88cf4e6622b3cb","body":{"detail":"connection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1363},"end":{"line":1368},"content_hash":"37faa7c25489c7bb21c58449a00b215ba4670c56c30156fd84acd0324fb5acb1"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","supersedes":"8a296aab4c5f337a8baa71e579c86e4effdc68efee4e1f7f666eaa14c81b7d91","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.879613Z","id":"6014047ed460f730c0d943908ca30e650fbc8a9a67e42512bb4345d3c23bbe94","body":{"detail":"note_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1552},"end":{"line":1556},"content_hash":"a0fa4a8c2b1a39edfb532ddd9c70fe377bd2d0458f5500bbff31400339dff010"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","supersedes":"b5db7a3a18966129939f1c920338dc94289b1dbbb3e4873d11df8d601d2da56f","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.880228Z","id":"16f45dd27f214d0b52cb92fc6e5dc8e1170f08366cf7ea2a7f350009f863f3c5","body":{"detail":"The overflow marker (install row approval_overflow:<approver>) lists the [author, artifact, thread] places whose routed content request_in held without a request, past MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) per approver or MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR (20) per author. Only Store::decide_request rechecks them, dropping a place once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request: answered by an open or declined request, delivered, gone, or now visible). A withdrawal or an approval made outside a decision changes nothing until the next decision, so the banner can outlive what it counted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1868},"end":{"line":1878},"content_hash":"73f004277ac55d0d5d175ac9d9633a7b394f8ae4a809ba5e85e370048b9398ee"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","supersedes":"b026f338e88573ca83778cc17fdfc5f46ca4112b78c4bffc1fde03dd2026501e","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.880865Z","id":"ac87751d1a8a52942ba49cc5a0775c7d47efaf8f2af9b32724233d490ef2834b","body":{"detail":"approve_owner_on_connect is the single approval made without a browser (spec section 21 item 3, M15). It is bounded to the connect: once per grant, within OWNER_ANSWER_SECS (10 minutes) of the tokens' issue, never once the person has made or revoked any approval of the owner (409 owner_answered, so a revocation in People stands; 409 answer_closed after the window), replays refused by accept_t first. Only the continuation token says it, never the access token agents sign with (crates/clax-server/tests/api_grants.rs a_connected_machine_approves_the_owner_through_its_continuation), and clax connect refuses on an agent channel (crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs connect_refuses_on_an_agent_channel). What remains: a process of the person's that reads remote.json within those ten minutes, before clax connect answers, could answer yes for them; the person can revoke it in People, and that revocation is final. Tests: store::people::tests::connecting_records_the_persons_approval_of_the_owner_once, the_answer_about_the_owner_never_overrides_the_person.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1476},"end":{"line":1568},"content_hash":"d5ef04715b7251bf982fd51818c94f17a2b0b3b2dd3450f46854211db24ca24d"},"summary":"The person's approval of the owner is recorded without a browser once, at connect: an agent present then could answer for the person","supersedes":"eb3fe53b5ebb95da0bd20d15a3fee0fb5479334999d96645e9da3f5a4bbf9166","tags":["security","spec:6.3","spec:21","M15","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.881448Z","id":"cbc85f9a803d271af33bf349533f7dddba36c4b96f24ceee8fe1611fb86a5a72","body":{"detail":"For flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1087},"end":{"line":1101},"content_hash":"a055d17fb6d13921d9565129c8f0b702f534ab8d657151596b97465c24004831"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","supersedes":"f9c8ae5247a5d12e7daf21e39eba8c58f4435b6dbc32b09960418576273645a3","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.882018Z","id":"d4465695e13ca070c8d7809b6bd2afd699cc78f1942dc4ca6a84f312706b25d1","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2107},"end":{"line":2118},"content_hash":"3661554d9ec3b6ade08fbb453c62e14c05eacd1871b109bac087e43dd7492399"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"f279547a08f03c884d9fb5356e98258bcf9059d31d99092b41a8077023532bf3","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T03:43:26.428090Z","id":"6292d07438c184087e19eb4a9957663976f112b2ac0792234acce14cd280061e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:751b305","summary":"Ruled by the coordinator: §14 wins, an end releases the thread. Spec 2026-10-08 §12's handoff rule no longer names an ended owner (751b305); check_may_hand_off_in keeps its branch for an owner row that is not live, which no end leaves.","supersedes":"2bca898d378c76a8059d4e3f0009909a5868aef84d8f9ce8038c7ba8847b6c17","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T03:43:26.428705Z","id":"6a7f5eb63fc6c741e97c0f26c722ba625443e14e28f57e6fdc84d61ed2cfdcb2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:751b305","summary":"Fixed as ruled: restore_note names the window that ended the session (5 minutes for a session without a grant, 30 with one), and §6.7 says so. cargo test -p clax-core --lib sessions::tests::cleanup::a_codex_session_restores_when_its_hook_names_it passes, asserting the local note's \"5 minutes\".","supersedes":"81ecb6e033ed72a41b9c8a14571de14b351bf4136503663425030820420d37ff","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T03:43:26.429212Z","id":"f374c559342886d3df8e939caf2a71b56de25537ecf5a4a7d6cb6b3436b7a90d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:751b305","summary":"Fixed as ruled: a send naming one agent that makes it the owner runs displace_owner_in, deleting the previous owner's undelivered rows of the thread and withdrawing its ask requests (reason thread_taken); @name keeps the earlier agents' rows (§11, §12 amended). cargo test -p clax-core --lib sessions::tests::cleanup::a_named_send_to_another_agent_displaces_the_old_owner passes, and fails with the call removed.","supersedes":"b9b20f8a9bc739486ce4f100f394298b7fb4a777cbb7f1a7578328cf14b21ccd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T03:43:26.429836Z","id":"6b05cc8e718566c0bd2531739ada737d768414a3503be59600c51b6f4a1f12c1","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §14 lists `person` (its person or the owner ended it) among the end reasons, and §6.7 and the tests treat it as one that restores nothing; but nothing ends a session with EndReason::Person (only its as_str/audit_reason arms name it). A person revoking their own grant ends its sessions `revoked`. Task 17, which owns People and per-agent rights, adds a browser route that ends one agent with EndReason::Person through Store::end_in.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1300},"end":{"line":1310},"content_hash":"56accea7079e7ececd175edc4952da35be68c1df9def95ef90794534057e4e90"},"summary":"EndReason::Person has no producer: no route lets a person or the owner end one agent; plan Task 17 (People, per-agent rights) adds the browser route","tags":["review","revisit:Task 17","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T03:43:34.698184Z","id":"cc657a87b355a01172099fad366279087250e8dd4d73650fbc7493d074721a03","body":{"detail":"state_of reports withheld (the target session's person as approver) from placeholder_at, which a take sets when it holds and tells a row, or while an open approval request of that person covers the row's comment author there (a send naming the agent, spec §10). A comment that joins no request (a send naming no agent, a later reply whose author has no open request there, an author held past the request limits) reads sent, waiting on its tier, until the agent's next take. Computing it from visibility at state time would build a Visibility per target session's person inside feedback_states_in, which listings call for every thread (spec §8.7 cost).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1907},"end":{"line":1916},"content_hash":"58070c3dc3bfd0816571f2b422f4f5498db2d6bcc2400ea7e8d12f9c3497b53f"},"summary":"A held row that no open request covers reads sent until a take holds it","supersedes":"7f7f58a66148f64f1e0b9354d4762f1a01db5a01863102b890f7fa709a79604d","tags":["people","spec:8.4","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T03:43:34.698931Z","id":"94285f387344cc5e2780991a92a1e777b279adc0774b19e43f4ed4acb5b8273e","body":{"detail":"release_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1432},"end":{"line":1448},"content_hash":"ed1cb058eed0b38a9d4e07ae6c733539b4ca4c1c6388d6f7a4614ccf4b5c1af2"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","supersedes":"fd9200fba44cd845dc8a0c3acaf5c9b7206f2d706842b11243812729f8f7410a","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T03:43:34.699606Z","id":"d1dcd98c6b93f08c945eb3f10844a11540fa51bfde1b0a84973137e587e7b5b1","body":{"detail":"An invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2051},"end":{"line":2062},"content_hash":"3661554d9ec3b6ade08fbb453c62e14c05eacd1871b109bac087e43dd7492399"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"d4465695e13ca070c8d7809b6bd2afd699cc78f1942dc4ca6a84f312706b25d1","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.813724Z","id":"b00f8f3b34bd3743dee054d554a2aca908864f9acb5a3a4751f5cc844c93ad67","body":{"detail":"withheld_in_thread counts the authors withheld from each comment body (the rows a take holds, spec M16). A thread whose comments the agent may see but whose anchor, clip or artifact title is another person's (spec §3.3 step 6) is delivered with those fields placeholdered and makes no request; the agent can ask for the artifact's content outside threads with ask {approval: {url_or_id}} (Store::ask_approval, withheld_outside_threads), which covers text fields, the current version, documents and assets, but not a thread's anchor.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1285},"end":{"line":1305},"content_hash":"2db7bc0ea49daabf8d49defd3d54488b8041d0c22a95068bc6531cfc23d68cee"},"summary":"Routing asks only for the authors of comment bodies; a withheld anchor, clip, batch note or title makes no request","supersedes":"d464a0943a57bf6a2f5f62391091b20241462ab70ef0b3994e99bb08c1051b74","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.814478Z","id":"ea1fcd06efb9ffa14ac30061358d3f922277ec079550f1f2827e63b6bd8c50d0","body":{"detail":"Spec §9.3: 'Declining keeps the rows held; a later ask there makes a new request only after 10 minutes'. request_in applies the same quiet period to routing, so a sender pressing Send again right after the approver declined does not re-announce the request; the rows are held and the agent's placeholder reads as not asked. If the owner wants a deliberate re-send to ask at once, drop the check for Cause::Routing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1111},"end":{"line":1120},"content_hash":"cf9707d61e55687d29484ea3ec1da7a8faa513bbca583c591bf81438ce7a4e23"},"summary":"A routed send within ten minutes of a decline makes no request, though spec §9.3 names only ask","supersedes":"a8e309e03984dc79e2fc898101fc66493599b0e0de4c628ff1c533559aa12189","tags":["people","spec:9.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.815116Z","id":"7247b1a205dbb5ea493ac46ad1a42645a731c5afe155b24006ed7e18dfe759b2","body":{"detail":"Registration derives a name from the repository and branch (spec section 11) without an event; session.start's body is harness, harness_session_id, cwd, transcript_path and pid. The first agent.name then reports previous: <derived name> with no earlier event naming it, and an @name in a comment cannot be tied to its session from the journal alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":174},"end":{"line":180},"content_hash":"2531645c1bbef5581474f3318cd70a2a599ab739af3be8223fbe8da994159a5b"},"suggested_fix":"Add name (classed as a name for redaction) to session.start and session.join bodies, and say so in audit spec section 6.8.","summary":"A session's derived name is never recorded, so agent.name's previous names a value the journal never held","supersedes":"2d5730fd1be34f1dad49416c48f9edf2fe8d5dab89bd35d49dc013a21c620780","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/store/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.815707Z","id":"0f0f13b253b8d8325d9ba5173c3b1bb2dc6c743bc19bd332167a9e10c2f467d3","body":{"detail":"The overflow marker (install row approval_overflow:<approver>) lists the [author, artifact, thread] places whose routed content request_in held without a request, past MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS (100) per approver or MAX_OPEN_PER_AUTHOR (20) per author. Only Store::decide_request rechecks them, dropping a place once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request: answered by an open or declined request, delivered, gone, or now visible). A withdrawal or an approval made outside a decision changes nothing until the next decision, so the banner can outlive what it counted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1897},"end":{"line":1907},"content_hash":"73f004277ac55d0d5d175ac9d9633a7b394f8ae4a809ba5e85e370048b9398ee"},"summary":"People's overflow banner stays up after withdrawals bring an approver under the limit, until their next decision","supersedes":"16f45dd27f214d0b52cb92fc6e5dc8e1170f08366cf7ea2a7f350009f863f3c5","tags":["people","spec:9.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
